The '''Burning Basement''' is one of the environments in [[chapter 1]] added in ''[[The Binding of Isaac: Afterbirth]]''. The theme of the Burning Basement is fire, and most enemies are replaced with burning versions. There are relatively few flying or shooting enemies; most of the enemies are ground-based and rely on contact damage. {{dlc|nr}} [[Rock]]s have a chance to be replaced with [[Fire Place]]s.

The Burning Basement's alternate floors are the {{s|Basement}} and the {{s|Cellar}}.

{{dlc|a+}} The Burning Basement is unlocked by defeating {{e|Mom's Heart}} 11 times.

{{dlc+|r}} After {{a|A Secret Exit}} is unlocked, a locked door similar to the one leading to a {{R|Treasure Room}} will appear in this floor's {{R|Boss Room}} upon defeating the boss leading to {{S|Downpour}} / {{S|Dross}}. Like a Treasure Room, this door requires a key to be unlocked. Unlike {{R|Angel Room}} and {{R|Devil Room}}s, this door never disappears.{{dlc-}}

